    "result_text": "All 294 tests pass, including `Cp19Tests`. \n\nThe change adds audit logging for successful owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`:\n\n- **A dedicated `AUDIT` logger** \u2014 `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`, matching the logger name the test captures.\n- **Logged after a successful save** so only successful creations are recorded (creations rejected by the quota/duplicate rules throw before reaching this point).\n- **Records the authenticated user, owner id, and membership number** \u2014 the user name is resolved from the Spring Security context via a `currentUsername()` helper (falling back to `\"anonymous\"` if unauthenticated).\n\nThe audit line produced is, e.g.: `Owner created by user=acceptance-admin ownerId=11 membershipNumber=11`.",
